{
  "name": "AI Content-Repurposing Engine (One Input -> Ten Outputs)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI Content-Repurposing Engine\n\n**One input -> ten outputs.** Drop a podcast / webinar recording into a watched Google Drive folder and this workflow:\n1. Downloads + transcribes it (Whisper)\n2. Extracts structured \"content atoms\" (themes, quotes, summary) via an AI Agent\n3. Fans out to 4 channel writers (LinkedIn, X thread, newsletter, short-form video captions)\n4. Runs a brand-safety filter\n5. Routes drafts to Slack for human approval\n6. Publishes approved posts and logs every variant to a Google Sheet\n\nAll credentials are references only -- add your own before running.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-160, -40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Parallel fan-out generation\nThe AI Agent output is sent to all four channel writers at once (single main output -> four targets). Each writer has its own channel-specific system prompt + shared brand-voice guidelines, so they run concurrently rather than in a slow chain.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "note-fanout",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Fan-out",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1520, -360]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Human-in-the-loop\nNothing auto-publishes blindly. Drafts are sanitized, checked against banned keywords, then posted to Slack. Execution pauses on the Wait node until a reviewer approves via the resume webhook. Only then do the publish nodes fire.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "note-approval",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Approval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [2760, -360]
    },
